1910.02373v2
Ridge Regression: Structure, Cross-Validation, and Sketching studies squared-error regression with a quadratic coefficient penalty and regularization selection through held-out or cross-validation error. The supplied frozen synopsis of sections 2 and 3 explains that ridge coefficients depend on feature covariance and regularization strength, and discusses validation bias in a high-dimensional asymptotic regime. This provides relevant context for selecting regularization after polynomial feature expansion. The synopsis contains no quantitative experimental results, so numerical performance, sketching benefits, or improvements cannot be reported from the available evidence. It also does not establish the optimal polynomial degree or alpha for this task. Those parameters must be evaluated on the supplied training and validation data using host-measured validation MSE; no local experimental measurements have yet been supplied.
