t test results, and the limited applicability of asymptotic literature to this finite task.",\n    "Abstract, introduction, methods, results, and discussion sections are all present."\n  ],\n  "Weaknesses": [\n    "The central empirical study is incomplete. Only one of 26 prescribed configurations has reported measurements, leaving the research question about weakly regularized quadratic structure versus polynomial alternatives unanswered.",\n    "There is no measured linear baseline, positive-regularization comparison, or higher-degree comparison. Consequently, the results establish neither the value of quadratic features nor the benefit of ridge regularization.",\n    "The submission offers no methodological novelty, and a single conventional regression fit provides insufficient empirical significance for a prestigious ML venue.",\n    "Reproducibility outside the trusted host is limited because feature scaling, intercept treatment, loss normalization, solver conventions, and implementation versions are undocumented in the submission.",\n    "The manuscript repeatedly restates the same baseline, protocol, and limitations across sections. This length obscures the small amount of empirical evidence and could be substantially reduced.",\n    "The agent-workflow references are peripheral to the regression question and are not supported by corresponding workflow experiments.",\n    "Execution verification and artifact availability are described, but the supplied manuscript does not expose sufficient implementation or artifact detail to independently assess those provenance claims."\n  ],\n  "Originality": 1,\n  "Quality": 2,\n  "Clarity": 2,\n  "Significance": 1,\n  "Questions": [\n    "Can the authors provide the actual host-measured validation MSEs for the remaining 19 initial configurations and the six subsequent alpha evaluations, together with the final configuration selected under the stated rule?",\n    "What prevented completion of the prescribed comparison, and should the submission be framed explicitly as a preliminary baseline report until those measurements are available?",\n    "What are the host\'s exact polynomial expansion, feature-scaling, intercept, penalty-normalization, and numerical-solver conventions?",\n    "Can the authors provide accessible execution identifiers or artifact references supporting the reported baseline and its stated independent verification?",\n    "After completing the prescribed comparisons, does positive regularization improve the quadratic candidate, and how does the selected candidate compare with the measured linear and higher-degree alternatives?",\n    "Can the manuscript be condensed and the peripheral workflow discussion removed so that the evidence and unresolved research question are easier to assess?"\n  ],\n  "Limitations": [\n    "The authors adequately disclose the principal limitation: only one configuration has reported execution evidence.",\n    "The fixed validation split supports only a comparison among evaluated candidates on those observations; repeated selection can produce optimistic validation estimates.",\n    "The adaptive refinement examines additional alpha values at only one degree and cannot establish a global optimum over the allowed parameter space.",\n    "Independent test performance, uncertainty estimates, and robustness across alternative samples are unavailable. These should remain unclaimed; additional datasets are not necessary to complete the assigned fixed-split experiment.",\n    "The dataset\'s provenance and intended application are insufficiently described to assess representativeness or application-specific societal consequences.",\n    "No concrete negative societal impact is apparent from the reported regression baseline, but broader deployment claims would require application context and assessment of consequential prediction errors."\n  ],\n  "Ethical Concerns": false,\n  "Soundness": 2,\n  "Presentation": 2,\n  "Contribution": 1,\n  "Overall": 3,\n  "Confidence": 4,\n  "Decision": "Reject"\n}\n```', True)
